{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1079721-2e-bale-hounds-and-other-lodges","id":1079721,"title":"[2E] Bale Hounds and other Lodges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-17T01:34:40-07:00","id":1079721,"title":"[2E] Bale Hounds and other Lodges","content":"I wonder how can work dynamics of Bale Hound becoming or being member of other, non-wicked Lodge? For example, I may have perfect NPCs pack for my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge\">Valkyries Mot</a> - only it's in the region where <i>all</i> Uratha are secretly Bale Hounds ( chronicles needs ). So those possible Valkyries, in secret, would be Bale Hounds. How could thing like this worked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:00:13-07:00","id":1079794,"title":"","content":"Since you can't be a member of multiple lodges, just have being a Bale Hound not be a Lodge thing.<br /> <br /> Though if <i>all </i>Uratha in the region are Bale Hounds, why would they bother to hide it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:59:54-07:00","id":1079817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1079721-2e-bale-hounds-and-other-lodges?p=1079794#post1079794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you can't be a member of multiple lodges, just have being a Bale Hound not be a Lodge thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going more with 'secret Tribe' option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1079721-2e-bale-hounds-and-other-lodges?p=1079794#post1079794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if <i>all </i>Uratha in the region are Bale Hounds, why would they bother to hide it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause you are part of greater Protectorate that is not all transformed to Hounds and you plan to make giant Wound in your city?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T20:56:20-07:00","id":1081273,"title":"","content":"I have a big problem with using <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1080462-2e-fan-lodge-of-shield\">Lodge of Shield</a> members as Bale Hounds. Would it be any possible with Ban of 'Must punish perpetrators of heinous crimes in your territory' - if the adherents of Lodge are those acts perpetrators in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T21:03:45-07:00","id":1081277,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds are known to commit heinous crimes, but you could argue that torturing lunes and corrupting loci aren't technically crimes.<br /> <br /> It would be hard to justify them doing more general Bale Hound things, like killing people or werewolves, without invoking the ban.<br /> <br /> You could make it a sort of knock-off lodge. The Lodge of the Tarnished Shield, headed up by a Maeltinet that encourages the corruption of law enforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:27:48-07:00","id":1095902,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about corrupting my Valkyrie Mot pack as part of Bale Hounds conspiracy in region. But from what I can tell, their Aspiration ( and connected Sacred Hunt ) will just work great with only changing part that sending souls to Odin for the Maeljins...<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> <i>To find and send souls of those high in Renowns \u2013 i.e. Uratha with Renown 3+ and humans or Wolf-Blooded that could would be marked by the deeds if they were Uratha </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T12:10:56-07:00","id":1095993,"title":"","content":"If you are a vast, open group of Uratha, the protectorate is probably formed to hunt you down.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, if the Bale Hounds are a tribe, EDIT: they can join other lodges-though I can't imagine them lingering there for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-23-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:15:04-07:00","id":1096045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1079721-2e-bale-hounds-and-other-lodges?p=1095993#post1095993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are a vast, open group of Uratha, the protectorate is probably formed to hunt you down.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, if the Bale Hounds are a tribe, EDIT: they can join other lodges-though I can't imagine them lingering there for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shift that premise on it's head, make Bale Hounds a Mot and now they can join both tribes and lodges and attempt to corrupt them from within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}